@using Triathlon.Web.Domain.Stats
@model IReadOnlyList<Kpi>
@*
    One row of KPI tiles: the home page's four-tile band (no ViewData) and the statistics page's
    ten-tile band ("wide" in ViewData).

    Two rulings live here.

    1. The number is real in the served HTML. The tile prints PublicText.Number(k.Value) as its
       first text node and keeps data-count for the counter; site.js resets that node to zero and
       tweens it only when motion is allowed, so a crawler, a printout, a no-JS visitor and a
       reduced-motion visitor all read the Federation's actual figures rather than "0".

    2. The band carries no discipline colour. Swim cyan on "Elite athletes" and run amber on
       "Race participations" made the colour code mean nothing; a KPI is not a discipline. The
       band is a timing board — one frame, hairline-divided cells, no per-cell stripe — so the
       numbers are the only thing on it that varies.
*@
@{
    var wide = ViewData["wide"] as bool? ?? false;
}
<div class="stat-band@(wide ? " wide" : "")">
@foreach (var k in Model)
{
    <div class="stat reveal">
      @if (k.Suffix is null)
      {
        <div class="stat-value mono" data-count="@k.Value">@Number(k.Value)@if (k.ShowPlus) {<span class="plus">+</span>}</div>
      }
      else
      {
        <div class="stat-value mono" data-count="@k.Value" data-suffix="@k.Suffix">@Number(k.Value)@k.Suffix@if (k.ShowPlus) {<span class="plus">+</span>}</div>
      }
      <div class="stat-label">@Bi(k.LabelEn, k.LabelAr)</div>
      @if (k.NoteEn is not null)
      {
        <div class="stat-note mono">@Bi(k.NoteEn, k.NoteAr ?? k.NoteEn)</div>
      }
    </div>
}
</div>
